# mod-loot-filter (2026-10 rework): rules sent over the window's protocol (`.lootfilter request`,
# the same handler the addon messages reach), loot through mod-auto-loot, and what each action
# leaves in the bags. Server-side test bot run (mod-fl-testbots), T1.
#
# Snapjaw (2408, the Hillsbrad river, always spawned) drops exactly one Turtle Meat (3712: white,
# trade goods / meat, stack 20, sells for 87c, no disenchant loot - storage-eligible); Rot Hide
# Brute (1939, Silverpine) always drops A Talking Head (3317: a white quest item, class 12, unique).
# (Wild Turkey 32820 was the first choice; its spawns belong to Pilgrim's Bounty.) The bot kills
# each creature next to itself with Death Touch (5); mod-auto-loot (10 yd, every 250 ms) loots it
# for the bot, and the filter acts one tick later. A looted corpse is gone about 3 s later
# (mod-auto-loot halves its time on every scan), so the next `pick` finds a living one. A loot that
# merges into a stack acts on the whole stack (unchanged behaviour).
#   b  one level-80 warrior; its rules are cleared at the start and at the end
name    mod-loot-filter - rules, loot, actions
timeout 240s

bot b warrior

place 0 -147.4 -1122.5 35
require b alive
do b destroy 3712
as b .lootfilter request X
expect output has "LFLS N|0"
as b .lootfilter request F|1
expect output has "LFLS F|1"
as b .lootfilter request C|2
expect output has "LFLS I|1|2|"

log 1 - a rule with two conditions sells the meat (white AND trade goods / meat)
as b .lootfilter request R|0|0|1|1|0:0:1:0:;3:0:7:8:
expect output has "LFLS R|"
expect output has "|1|1|1|0:0:1:0:;3:0:7:8:"
expect output has "LFLS N|1"
pick t1 creature:2408 near b
require t1 alive
do b approach t1
do b cast 5 on t1 triggered
waitfor t1 dead timeout 5s
wait 2s
waitfor t1 missing timeout 15s
expect b item 3712 == 0
as b .lootfilter stats
expect output has "Rules: 1"
expect output has "Gold earned"

log 2 - TO STORAGE deposits it (the type condition with any subclass)
as b .lootfilter request X
as b .lootfilter request R|0|0|4|1|3:0:7:255:
expect output has "LFLS N|1"
pick t2 creature:2408 near b
require t2 alive
do b approach t2
do b cast 5 on t2 triggered
waitfor t2 dead timeout 5s
wait 2s
waitfor t2 missing timeout 15s
expect b item 3712 == 0
log 2b - what the core wrote reads back from the DB (the rule and the statistics batch)
as b .lootfilter reload
expect output has "Rules reloaded (1 rules)"
as b .lootfilter request G
expect output has "|1|4|1|3:0:7:255:"
expect output has "LFLS N|1"
as b .lootfilter stats
expect output value Stored >= 1

log 2c - DISENCHANT on an item without disenchant loot stores it, as the old fallback did
as b .lootfilter request X
as b .lootfilter request R|0|0|2|1|6:0:3712:0:
pick t7 creature:2408 near b
require t7 alive
do b approach t7
do b cast 5 on t7 triggered
waitfor t7 dead timeout 5s
wait 2s
waitfor t7 missing timeout 15s
expect b item 3712 == 0

log 3 - KEEP leaves the meat in the bags (no deposit any more)
as b .lootfilter request X
as b .lootfilter request R|0|0|0|1|3:0:7:255:
pick t3 creature:2408 near b
require t3 alive
do b approach t3
do b cast 5 on t3 triggered
waitfor t3 dead timeout 5s
wait 2s
waitfor t3 missing timeout 15s
expect b item 3712 == 1

log 4 - the bag scan acts on nothing and names the KEEP rule for the meat
as b .lootfilter request S
expect output has "LFLS S|"
expect output has "|0|1|3712"
expect output has "LFLS Z|"
expect b item 3712 == 1

log 5 - a switched-off KEEP on top does not protect; DELETE takes the whole stack
as b .lootfilter request X
as b .lootfilter request R|0|0|3|1|0:2:1:0:
as b .lootfilter request R|0|1|0|0|6:0:3712:0:
expect output has "LFLS N|2"
expect output has "LFLS R|"
pick t4 creature:2408 near b
require t4 alive
do b approach t4
do b cast 5 on t4 triggered
waitfor t4 dead timeout 5s
wait 2s
waitfor t4 missing timeout 15s
expect b item 3712 == 0

log 6 - the same KEEP switched on protects the meat from the DELETE below it
as b .lootfilter request X
as b .lootfilter request R|0|0|3|1|0:2:1:0:
as b .lootfilter request R|0|1|0|1|6:0:3712:0:
pick t5 creature:2408 near b
require t5 alive
do b approach t5
do b cast 5 on t5 triggered
waitfor t5 dead timeout 5s
wait 2s
waitfor t5 missing timeout 15s
expect b item 3712 == 1

log 7 - filter off: nothing happens, even under a DELETE rule
as b .lootfilter request X
as b .lootfilter request R|0|0|3|1|0:2:1:0:
as b .lootfilter request F|0
expect output has "LFLS F|0"
pick t6 creature:2408 near b
require t6 alive
do b approach t6
do b cast 5 on t6 triggered
waitfor t6 dead timeout 5s
wait 2s
waitfor t6 missing timeout 15s
expect b item 3712 == 2

log 7b - a quest item is never touched, even under a DELETE rule
as b .lootfilter request F|1
place 0 705 610 45
do b destroy 3317
pick g1 creature:1939 near b
require g1 alive
do b approach g1
do b cast 5 on g1 triggered
waitfor g1 dead timeout 5s
wait 2s
waitfor g1 missing timeout 15s
expect b item 3317 == 1

log 8 - invalid requests are refused
as b .lootfilter request R|0|0|9|1|0:0:1:0:
expect output has "LFLS !|invalid"
as b .lootfilter request R|0|0|1|1|7:0:0:0:a;b
expect output has "LFLS !|invalid"
as b .lootfilter request R|0|0|1|1|3:1:4:255:
expect output has "LFLS !|invalid"
as b .lootfilter request T|0|17
expect output has "LFLS !|noitem"

cleanup
as b .lootfilter request X
as b .lootfilter request F|1
as b .lootfilter request C|1
do b destroy 3712
do b destroy 3317
log loot_filter done
